WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
11 gene reprogramming was given to people before any published human data. This is Longevity Weekly,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:13.140
Episode 3. The science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. Fight aging describes

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.880
that use as partial epigenetic reprogramming carried by adenine associated viral vectors,

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:25.420
given to a small number of people through medical tourism manufacture, including a triple helix science

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:31.740
effort. The outlet says this was not the first patient in life biosciences optic neuropathy trial,

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:38.640
which it calls recently launched. The K-HL Foundation tied to Kenneth Scott, born 1942,

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:45.580
and Helga Sands, born 1938, is presented as pushing rejuvenation tools toward people who want

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:52.420
them now. Christine Scott received the experimental construct described as 11 genes and as containing

00:00:54.120 --> 00:01:03.160
OCT4, SOX2, and KLF4 on March 11, 2026. It was given under the Mucosa, with thinking and

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:08.580
memory named as the main target, and the factors expression is described as switched on by a

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.460
doxy-cycline approach. No schedule belongs in this telling, and no published human study here

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.680
establishes composition, safety, effect, or any regulators approval for aging.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:28.100
Compound 991, a drug that turns on AMPK directly, lengthened life in fruit flies, nematode worms,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.260
and fission yeast.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:35.240
That is a pre-clinical result in short-lived species reported by a fight aging from a

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:35.900
journal paper.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.100
In mice, the same compound produced what the authors call a pro-longgevity protein profile,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.800
not a reported gain in mouse lifespan.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.980
The commentary calls the life extension modest

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.900
and argues these species answer metabolic tweaks

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.440
more readily than humans do.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.800
The piece also says Metformin hits AMPK indirectly

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:01.280
by shifting the cells AMP, ADP, and ATP balance,

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.760
and that animal results on that indirect path are mixed.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.540
No human outcome and no aging approval for compound 991

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:10.460
is in the report.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:19.080
George Mazanakis, 54, died on September 9th, 2026, after cardiac arrest at a colonnackie clinic

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.440
where he had an appointment for plasma ferrisis sold as anti-aging care.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:29.740
Ecosylia is reporting an investigation, not a trial of whether plasma exchange slows aging.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:36.660
Elpus hospital said he arrived at 4.45 in the afternoon, with no spontaneous breathing or pulse,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:43.040
and death was pronounced at 540. The two doctors deny wrongdoing and say he lost consciousness

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.820
before treatment. The outlet says investigators dispute that.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.800
As of September 24th, both were in pretrial detention on homicide charges, which is

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.900
not a finding of guilt.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:03:01.360
On October 6th, Family Lawyer, Charles Ambos-Licutus, said toxicology and histology were still pending.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:07.580
Health Minister Adonis Georgiades said the clinic's internal medicine license did not cover plasma

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:12.420
ferrisis, and the death prompted the government to announce a new rulebook for these centers.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.940
The same report says an appointment and a cardiac arrest, in that order,

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:22.940
do not by themselves prove the procedure caused the death. A review summarized by fight aging

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:28.200
treats osteoporosis and neurodegenerative disease as lightly sharing upstream damage,

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.640
average, rather than one simply causing the other.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.920
That is a synthesis of existing evidence, not a new human trial, and not a measured

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:36.660
drug effect.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:43.280
The process it names is inflamaging, chronic, low-grade, sterile inflammation driven by

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.900
senescent cells and the chemicals they keep releasing.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:52.480
Directly measured maximal oxygen uptake, taken during a cardiopulmonary exercise test,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.100
is the gold standard reading of cardiorespiratory fitness, and that measure is this week's

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:04.760
mechanism. A 2009 meta-analysis in JAMA turned that capacity into metabolic equivalents

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:09.820
and treated one metabolic equivalent as about one kilometer an hour faster running

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:17.220
or jogging. Newer work often estimates the number. One 2026 UK biobank paper used two

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:23.500
sub-maximal bite tests. Another estimated fitness from how heart rate answered a rising workload.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:30.160
A 2010 review says proposed biology links higher fitness to insulin sensitivity, blood

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.760
lipids, body composition, inflammation, and blood pressure.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.380
Those are suggestions in a review, not a path proved in an experiment.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:44.760
A 2026 observational molecular paper found higher fitness lining up with quieter signals

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:51.040
for inflammation, triglyceride handling, glycolysis, and vessel dysfunction, and louder

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:57.380
signals for cholesterol transport, apple-lipoprotein particle size, and cytoskeletal remodeling.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.820
Blood correlates are not a lifespan mechanism.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.000
The heaviest human evidence is still observation, pooled.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:16.000
That 2009 meta-analysis combined 33 cohorts, 102,980 people, and 6,910 deaths for mortality

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:24.880
from any cause, and 84,300 23 people, and 4,485 coronary or cardiovascular cases.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:31.960
Each extra metabolic equivalent of capacity went with a relative risk of 0.87 for death

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:42.740
from any cause, interval 0.84 to 0.90, and 0.85 for those events, interval 0.82 to 0.88.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:50.520
8. Low fitness versus high carried a relative risk of 1.70 for death from any cause, interval

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:58.960
1.51 to 1.92. People at 7.9 metabolic equivalents or above had substantially lower rates

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:06.220
than people under that mark. A 2015 meta-analysis in annals of oncology, six perspective studies,

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:16.120
701,654 people, 2002 cancer deaths, median follow-up 16.4 years, found a graded inverse

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.520
link with death from cancer overall. Against low fitness, the middle group had a summary

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:34.900
relative risk of 0.80, interval 0.67-0.97, and the high group 0.55, interval 0.47-0.65, adjusting

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:40.960
for body fat left a similar pattern, a 2017 review says that inverse pattern held whether

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:47.220
studies measured oxygen uptake directly, estimated it from an exercise test, or used an equation

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:53.560
with no exercise test. It also notes the American Heart Association had urged routine fitness checks

00:06:53.560 --> 00:07:01.340
as a clinical vital sign, which is a professional position, not a drug approval. A 1996 JAMA clinic cohort

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:07.460
put 25,341 men and 7,080 women through a maximal test.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:18.920
There were 601 deaths in 211,996 man-years and 89 deaths in 52,982 woman-years, low fitness

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:28.820
state independent, adjusted relative risk 1.52 in men, interval 1.28 to 1.82 and 2.10 in women,

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:32.080
Interval 1.36-3.21

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:36.880
In women, smoking was the other independent predictor the paper flagged.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:42.320
Relative risk 1.99-1.25-3.17

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:48.320
Death rates still fell across fitness categories inside groups split by smoking, cholesterol,

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.840
blood pressure, and health.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:55.740
Fit people who smoked or who had high blood pressure or high cholesterol had lower adjusted

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.540
to death rates than unfit people with none of those traits.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.200
A 2010 review says earlier studies find fitness

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.220
appears to blunt the extra death risk tied to obesity.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.940
Nobody in these cohorts was assigned

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.160
their fitness by lottery.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:14.400
In 2026, 11,530 UK bio bank adults,

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:19.160
ages 40 to 73, each with two sub-maximal tests,

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.540
no prior cardiovascular disease,

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:30.840
and early events set aside were followed a median 14.0 years, inter-cortile range 13.0 to 14.6.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:37.180
Models adjusted for starting fitness, social and lifestyle factors, genetic predisposition,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:44.560
change in body mass index and physical activity. Counts were 921 new cardiovascular events

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.540
and 119 cardiovascular deaths.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:51.180
Each extra milliliter per kilogram per minute per year

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.580
of estimated maximal oxygen uptake

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.780
went with a hazard ratio of 0.85 for new disease.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:05.000
Interval 0.75 to 0.96 and 0.66 for cardiovascular death.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.400
Interval 0.51 to 0.87.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.260
The authors call the pattern roughly linear

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:14.520
with no threshold, and declines went the other way.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:21.540
Metabolomic and proteomic signatures of fitness are squared about 0.50 to 0.60,

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:31.060
or checked in 354,222 people, with metabolite data and 29,961 with protein data.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:40.440
Over about 9 years and 27,659 deaths, the metabolite signature lined up with a 39-54% lower

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:47.100
risk of death from any cause, a 90% lower type 2 diabetes risk in both discovery and validation,

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:54.980
a 42% to 47% lower cardiovascular risk, and a 33% to 39% lower colorectal cancer

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:55.420
risk.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:02.400
The protein signature lined up with a 17% lower death risk and a 22% to 39% lower risk

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.440
of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:12.600
studies, after adjustment for age, sex, ethnicity, socioeconomic status, smoking, alcohol, diet,

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.900
body mass index, and relevant medical history.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.740
Cause is not shown.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:22.180
Sickness can pull a fitness score down and risk up at the same time.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.840
An estimate is not a gas measurement.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.600
A signature is not an outcome, and the outcome links are still associations.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.640
Intervals on the rare deaths are wide.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:39.180
These papers do not report a regulator approving fitness testing or exercise as an aging treatment.

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:45.440
After starting fitness is already in the model, a yearly rise of 1 milliliter per kilogram per

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:51.580
minute in the estimate still lines up with lower cardiovascular risk, and that lineup does not show

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:56.940
that producing the rise will produce the drop. One thing worth knowing is that a fitness change

00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:02.260
still tracking with later heart disease in an observational cohort that already accounted for

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:07.640
the starting score is a sharper description than a single label, and it is still not cause.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:14.180
Fewer cancer deaths in higher fitness categories across prospective observational studies do

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:17.680
not peel fitness apart from the rest of the life that produced the score.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:23.980
An anti-aging appointment and a cardiac arrest the same afternoon in investigative reporting

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.520
do not establish what the procedure did.

